# Unanchored on purpose. The anchored form does not cover fuzz/target, which is how two hundred megabytes of object files end up committed.
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.profraw
.DS_Store

# Sweep output pulled back off a bench host for the scoreboard. The committed copy lives in bench/ and is the one SCOREBOARD.md is generated from; anything else here is scratch.
/scratch

# What the fuzzers accumulate. A corpus grows without bound and is worth keeping, just not here; an artifact is a crashing input, which belongs in a test the moment anybody looks at it.
/fuzz/corpus
/fuzz/artifacts

# Names the bench machines. It stays out of a public repository for the same reason it does in cache-bench, and ci.yml fails if it is ever tracked.
hosts.toml
